The one change in salmobase's own repository (https://gitlab.com/elixir-nmbu/salmobase) for the functional SNP portal:
a block in its Apache file that sends /snp to the portal's container. docs/SALMOBASE.md says how it becomes a merge
request there. Made against salmobase's master at 9b1f40e (2026-10-28); it applies to its dev branch as well.
In a clone of salmobase:  git apply <this file>

diff --git a/server_config/apache2/salmobase.conf b/server_config/apache2/salmobase.conf
index ea4066e..c4d58d7 100644
--- a/server_config/apache2/salmobase.conf
+++ b/server_config/apache2/salmobase.conf
@@ -30,6 +30,21 @@ ServerName ${SERVER_NAME}
     	ProxyPassReverse http://docs:80/
 	</Location>
 
+	# The functional SNP portal (https://github.com/garethgillard/salmo-snp): a container of its own, on this
+	# network under the name `snp`. Its pages, forms and static files are all under /snp/. disablereuse: the name is
+	# looked up for each request, so a new container of the portal is found without a restart here. The portal's
+	# answers do not carry the JBrowse CORS headers set above. While no such container runs, /snp answers an error
+	# and nothing else changes.
+	<Location /snp>
+		ProxyPass http://snp:8000/snp timeout=300 disablereuse=On
+		ProxyPassReverse http://snp:8000/snp
+		RequestHeader set X-Forwarded-Proto "https"
+		LimitRequestBody 314572800
+		Header onsuccess unset Access-Control-Allow-Origin
+		Header onsuccess unset Access-Control-Allow-Headers
+		Header onsuccess unset Access-Control-Expose-Headers
+	</Location>
+
 	ProxyPass /datafiles !
 	ProxyPass /static !
 	ProxyPass / http://127.0.0.1:8000/
